       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one. I know you've confirmed it, but 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. The risks are serious: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. They rise with dose and aren't offset by normal kidney and liver function. Entering it as written could lead to real harm, so I'd rather not do it.\n\nHere is what I can enter right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note about the indication and planned duration.\n- **Any lower dose** you prefer.\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than that, a clinical pharmacist can help with multimodal options. Examples are scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or a different agent.\n\nIf you think I've misread the order, for example if it was meant as a total daily dose, tell me and I'll enter the corrected version. If you still want the 1,600 mg dose, you'll need to enter it directly in the order system, where pharmacy verification applies."
      }
